                     <provenance source="3442"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_295">Lanthony
                           (secunda), Gloucestershire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin and
                           St John the Baptist</orgName><p>On fol. 114v at top: "Iste liber est d[.
                           . .] prioris Lanth. prime." Below this (s. xv): "Morganus", and
                           contents.</p><p>London, B.L., Royal 2 C.x; Lambeth Palace 30; 80, fols.
                           168--244; 101; 138, fols. 1--44; 148; 153, fols. 156--179; 165, fols.
                           102--190; 195; 200, fols. 114--163; 208; 215; 218, fols. 1--89; 227; 231;
                           345, fols. 97--227; 360, fols. 1--118; 365, fols. 1--119; 377; 378, fols.
                           i, ii, 1--56, 125--165; 390; 394; 397; 398; 409; 449; 452; 481; Oxford,
                           Bodl. 839, Hatton 49, Corpus Christi Coll. 33, 43; Trinity Coll. 39 have
                           a note of contents in the hand of 'Morganus canonicus de Kermerden' (s.
                           xv), who has written his name in many of the books.</p><p
                        > </p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="#i" source="6706"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_327"
                           >Llanthony (prima), Monmouthshire. Augustinian priory of St John the
                           Baptist; cell of Lanthony (secunda) from AD 1481</orgName><p>On fol. 114v
                           at top: "Iste liber est d[. . .] prioris Lanth. prime." Below this (s.
                           xv): "Morganus", and contents, relating its later history to Lanthony
                           secunda (q.v.).</p></provenance>
                  </history>
